dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?D\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u65294 ?}{\uc1 \u26631 ?}{\uc1 \u35760 ?}{\uc1 \u20043 ?}{\uc1 \u38388 ?}{\uc1 \u21487 ?}{\uc1 \u20197 ?}{\uc1 \u20132 ?}{\uc1 \u21449 ?}{\uc1 \u23884 ?}{\uc1 \u22871 ?}}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?For nearly ten years, the Unified Modeling Language (UML) has been the industry standard for visualizing, specifying, constructing, and documenting the }{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?71 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  of a software-intensive system. As the }{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?72 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  standard modeling language, the UML facilitates communication and reduces confusion among project }{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?73 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  . The recent standardization of UML 2.0 has further extended the language's scope and viability. Its inherent expressiveness allows users to }{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?74 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  everything from enterprise information systems and distributed Web-based applications to real-time embedded systems.}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? The UML is not limited to modeling software. In fact, it is expressive enough to model }{\fs24 \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \ul1  \uc1 \u160 ?75 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  systems, such as workflow in the legal system, the structure and behavior of a patient healthcare system, software engineering in aircraft combat systems, and the design of hardware.}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1  \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? To understand the UML, you need to form a conceptual model of the language, and this requires learning three major elements: the UML's basic building blocks, the rules that dictate how those building blocks may be put together, and some common mechanisms that apply throughout the UML.}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 71\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. classes \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \loch \af4 \hich \af4 \dbch \f1 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \cf1   }{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 B. components \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \loch \af4 \hich \af4 \dbch \f1 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \cf1  }{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 C. sequences \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?D. artifacts}{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \dbch \af1 \hich \af3 \loch \af3 \cf1 {\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 72\dbch \f5 {\uc1 \u12289 ?} A. real \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? }{\fs24 \loch \af4 \hich \af4 \dbch \f1 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \cf1    }{\fs24 \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf1 B. legal \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ? \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \loch \af4 \hich \af4 \dbch \f